  "reason": "The completed RNA-only singleprofile experiments show that scvi_n200 outperforms pca_n2000 on both accuracy and F1, suggesting scvi is the more promising RNA representation. However, it is still unclear whether using multiple profiles with aggregation improves performance over a single profile. config_005 keeps the best-performing RNA encoder and changes only the profile setting and aggregation to multiprofile with simple avgpool, isolating the effect of multiprofile aggregation. This is a high-value next experiment because it exploits the current best RNA direction while testing an important untested design choice before adding image or transformer complexity."
